.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-LIST" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-list - List durable tunnels


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List durable tunnels

.PP
List durable tunnels visible to this account with cursor and limit pagination. Select an exact tunnel for show, status, routes, domains, or lifecycle commands.

.PP
Durable tunnels retain identity, routes, connectors, and domains across client sessions. Ephemeral tunnels have a separate lifecycle. Route publication and browser HTTP access require exact authorization; TLS for browser HTTP terminates at the edge.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--cursor\fP=""
	continue a previous page

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=100
	maximum results (1-200)

.PP
\fB--owner\fP=""
	filter owner: mine, shared, or an authorized account ID

.PP
\fB--q\fP=""
	filter by resource name or ID

.PP
\fB--state\fP=""
	filter by resource state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel(1)\fP
